The meetings endpoints (POST /meetings, PUT /meetings/{domain}/{id}, GET /meetings/{domain}/{id}, GET /meetings/list) expose a `link` field on the meeting object starting at API version V19: an https join link carrying the meeting's live join code as `key`/`code` query parameters (`<base>/meeting-join/?key=<codeKey>&code=<codeValue>&domain=<domain>`). The field is present only when the meeting has a live join code; it is omitted otherwise (e.g. meetings created before this change, deployments whose code store cannot hold meeting codes, or multi-ingress deployments with no join-link URI configured for the user's domain). The V15-V18 endpoint shapes are unchanged.
